$$$

|!Color|!Meaning|
|@@background-color:#6c757d;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Actor|Person or system triggering/receiving the flow|
|@@background-color:#0d6efd;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Trigger|Event that initiates a pipeline stage|
|@@background-color:#198754;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Stage|Automated pipeline step|
|@@background-color:#fd7e14;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Gate|Manual approval or decision required|
|@@background-color:#dc3545;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Warning|Failure or notification path|

---

!! Syntax

```
flowchart TD
    nodeId[Rectangle] --> nodeId2{Diamond}
    nodeId2 -->|label| nodeId3([Stadium])
    nodeId3 --> nodeId4[(Cylinder)]

    classDef myClass fill:#color,stroke:#color,color:#fff
    nodeId:::myClass
```

''Direction:'' `TD` (top-down), `LR` (left-right), `BT` (bottom-top), `RL` (right-left)

|!Shape syntax|!Shape|
|`[Text]`|Rectangle|
|`{Text}`|Diamond (decision)|
|`(Text)`|Rounded rectangle|
|`([Text])`|Stadium|
|`[(Text)]`|Cylinder (database)|
|`((Text))`|Circle|

!! Tips

* Use `flowchart` (not the legacy `graph`) — the modern keyword supports all node shapes and subgraphs.
* Quote any node with the label `end` as `["End State"]` to avoid a parser conflict.
* Apply `classDef` categories to group nodes by meaning and pair with a legend table.
* `%%{init: {"flowchart": {"curve": "monotoneX"}}}%%` on the first line inside the `$$$` block selects a smoother edge curve.
* See also: [[State Diagram]] for state machines, [[Sequence Diagram]] for actor interactions.

